result=dict(status='PASS_REVIEWED_CROSS_VERSION_NUMERICS',image_id=r['image_id'],policy_sha256=r['policy_sha256'],source_measurement_sha256=sha(q/'cross-version-quality.json'),matched_state_sha256=sha(q/'replay-campaign.json'),kernel_gates_sha256=sha(root/'kernels-final/campaign.json'),review=dict(short_bitidentity=False,old_bitidentity_check_status='FAILED_RETAINED_NOT_RELABELLED',short_ppl=d['short']['perplexity'],stored_short_ppl=d['stored_v2']['short']['perplexity'],short_top1_agreement=d['short']['top1_agreement'],stored_short_top1_agreement=d['stored_v2']['short']['top1_agreement'],numerical_changes=d['changes'],rationale='Engineering review of this explicitly hashed measurement: the same-runtime v2 bitidentity test is not satisfied across the upstream Torch/vLLM upgrade and remains a failed recorded check. On unchanged stored BF16 references, short PPL improves 0.125% and 32K-suffix PPL 0.321%; short JS, reverse KL and KL tails improve. Mean short KL increases 0.000872 and long KL 0.000129. BF16-relative top1 agreement changes from 492/512 to 490/512 short probes and stays 8/8 long probes. These are mixed distribution changes, not a claim of identical output or a general quality improvement. Independently referenced kernel math and all four actual-state replay cases pass the unchanged tolerances, including full-graph C4 and long prefill. Accept the bounded upgrade numerics with these explicit limitations; no attention tolerance was relaxed.',limits='Finite engineered panels; stored references reused without executing old runtime or original BF16 model. Old and new isolated JIT caches can produce different floating-point execution choices; cause of every cross-version token difference is not proven. API, resource and performance gates are still required.'))
